domain CompactPsycheRepairSchemaFailure:
  description |
    Identify why the approved replay stopped when bounded semantic repair could
    not recover a malformed Compact V2 expression brief.

problem P1:
  |
    The repeat-capable third turn returned expressionBrief under delta. The one
    permitted repair then returned appraisal fields in
    replacement.expressionBrief and failed strict application validation.

premise P2:
  |
    Structured provider output is not guaranteed. The bounded repair call must
    contain the complete contract needed to construct every required
    replacement object without relying on hidden chat history.

evidence E1:
  |
    The initial Compact V2 system prompt explicitly states that expressionBrief
    is a top-level sibling of delta and gives all field names, enum values, and
    focus cardinality.

evidence E2:
  |
    The failed initial provider response placed expressionBrief under delta.
    Decoding removed that unrecognized delta field and application validation
    reported top-level expressionBrief as required.

evidence E3:
  |
    The repair call is a separate Chat Completions request. Its system prompt
    said only expressionBrief complete object and did not state the six field
    names, enum domains, focus cardinality, or value types.

evidence E4:
  |
    The repair request carried rejectedSemanticSlice.expressionBrief as null,
    so the request contained neither a valid example nor the missing object
    contract. It did include the invalid path and writable root.

evidence E5:
  |
    The repair response copied speech-appraisal-shaped fields into
    replacement.expressionBrief. Strict repair validation rejected sourceThread
    and focus types and unrecognized appraisal keys.

evidence E6:
  |
    Existing repair tests supplied an already valid expressionBrief object as
    a mocked repair response. They did not require the repair prompt to contain
    the expressionBrief schema and did not cover recovery from a missing brief.

evidence E7:
  |
    The correction adds the complete replacement object contract to the repair
    prompt and a missing-expressionBrief regression. The focused backend suite,
    backend typecheck, lizard, and DSL audit pass after the correction.

decision D1 based_on P1, P2, E1, E2:
  |
    Initial defect cause: this provider sample violated the explicit top-level
    output contract. The model-internal reason for that deviation is unknown.

decision D2 based_on P1, P2, E3, E4, E5:
  |
    Root cause of bounded-repair failure: the independent repair request omitted
    the required expressionBrief structural contract while the rejected slice
    contained no brief to preserve. The repair request was under-specified for
    the required replacement and produced an invalid shape.

decision D3 based_on E6:
  |
    Escape cause: mocked repair tests injected a valid replacement directly and
    verified merge behavior, but did not test the prompt contract or the
    missing-expressionBrief repair case.

decision D4 based_on D2, D3, E7:
  |
    Corrective action: include the complete speechAppraisal and expressionBrief
    shapes in the repair system prompt and retain regression coverage for prompt
    completeness and recovery from a missing expressionBrief. Any new provider
    replay must use a new immutable run ID and separate approval.

